st - manage stacked diffs on top of git

usage: st <command> [args]

commands:
  abort       Abort an in-progress restack/rebase, restoring the prior state
  bottom      Jump to the bottom branch of the current stack (just above trunk)
  checkout    Check out a tracked branch (lists branches if no name)
  completion  Print a shell completion script (bash|zsh|fish)
  continue    Resume a restack that was interrupted by a merge conflict
  create      Create a new branch stacked on the current branch
  delete      Delete a branch and re-parent its children
  down        Move down the stack toward trunk
  fold        Fold the current branch into its parent (parent absorbs its commits)
  guide       Print the recommended stacked-diff workflow
  init        Initialize stacked stack tracking in this repo
  log         Show the stack as a tree
  modify      Amend (or add) a commit on the current branch and restack everything above
  onto        Move the current branch (and its upstack) onto a new parent
  rename      Rename a branch and update the stack metadata
  repair      Reconcile the stack metadata with the repository (fix drift)
  restack     Rebase the current branch and everything above it onto their parents
  squash      Squash all of the current branch's commits into one
  status      Show current branch, its parent/children, and restack state
  submit      Push every branch in the current stack to the remote (no PRs — login-free)
  sync        Fetch trunk, fast-forward it, restack everything, and prune merged branches
  top         Jump to the top of the current stack
  track       Start tracking the current git branch in the stack
  undo        Undo the last stack-mutating command
  untrack     Stop tracking a branch (re-parents its children)
  up          Move up the stack to a child branch
  validate    Check the stack state for drift or inconsistencies
  help        show this help
  version     print the version
